cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this repository helps you, you may cite it as below. It is an informal,
  work-in-progress synthesis of published research, written with Claude, an AI
  assistant by Anthropic. It is not an official standard, not peer-reviewed,
  and not a new result.
title: "presentations (work in progress, parked)"
abstract: >-
  How to build a presentation, academic or business, so that it is cheap
  to follow and to remember. An extension of reader-ergonomics: the
  evidence particular to presentations.
  Use it as a reading list and a starting point, not as an authority.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tewf"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tewf/presentations"
license:
